+// A privileged opcode that raises an exception can be continued by a guest
+// exception handler (AlphaROM/Settec does exactly that for ICEBP).  In that case
+// execution must carry on at the instruction after the trapping opcode, which is
+// what the interpreter's main loop does on its own (it assigns R_RIP = addr
+// right after EmitSignal() returns).  Without this, the block that gets
+// re-dispatched keeps re-executing the same faulting opcode forever.
+#define RESUME_AFTER_TRAP   if(dyn->need_reloc) TABLE64(xRIP, addr); else MOV64x(xRIP, addr)
